  <h1>Emergency Boiler Callout Prices in York: What You'll Actually Pay</h1>
  <p>Boiler's gone, house is getting cold, and the last thing you want is to ring round three companies and get "it depends" from all of them. So here's the number: our <a href="/boiler-repairs-breakdowns/">emergency boiler repair</a> call-out in York is £120. That's what you pay, no VAT to add on top.</p>

  <h2>What the £120 actually covers</h2>
  <p>That fee covers the visit and a proper diagnosis. An engineer comes to your house, has a look at what's wrong with your boiler, and tells you straight what's caused it. It's not a foot-in-the-door fee that balloons once someone's stood in your kitchen. If the fault turns out to be something quick, a reset, a pressure problem, a stuck valve, that £120 is often the whole bill.</p>

  <h2>What's included in the visit</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>An engineer travelling out to you, not a call centre reading from a script</li>
    <li>A proper diagnosis, not a guess based on what you've described over the phone</li>
    <li>A plain-English explanation of what's happened and why</li>
    <li>A written price for any further work, before anything else is touched</li>
  </ul>
  <p>That's the point of a fixed call-out fee. You know what you're paying just to get someone qualified out to look at the problem, separate from whatever the fix ends up costing.</p>

  <h2>Why we don't do the "cheap callout, big invoice" trick</h2>
  <p>Plenty of people ringing about a boiler not working in York have been caught out before. Quoted a low number to get someone through the door, then hit with a much bigger bill once the engineer's already in and they feel stuck. We do it the other way round. One clear call-out price, and if you need parts or further work, that gets priced and agreed with you first, not after. You get a written quote, you say yes or no, and only then do we carry on.</p>

  <h2>When it costs more than £120</h2>
  <p>When the job needs more than diagnosis and a quick fix. If a part's failed and needs replacing, or the repair takes longer than a standard visit, that extra cost is quoted and agreed with you before it's added to the bill. Now and then a breakdown shows the boiler's on its last legs rather than worth patching up again. If that's the case, we'll say so, rather than keep charging you to repair something that won't hold up long-term.</p>

  <h2>Same-day boiler repair, same price</h2>
  <p>Whether it's a same day boiler repair because you've got no heating in York on a freezing morning, or something that can wait for a normal appointment, the £120 doesn't change depending on how urgent it feels. We'd rather you knew the real number before you pick up the phone than find out afterwards.</p>

  <h2>If someone vulnerable is affected, say so</h2>
  <p>A good number of the calls we get are from people worried about an elderly parent, a young family, or someone unwell being left without heating, not just about the money. If that's your situation, tell us when you ring. It doesn't change the £120, but it does change how we prioritise getting to you.</p>

  <h2>Get a straight answer, no obligation</h2>
  <p>If your boiler's broken down and you want to know roughly what you're looking at before booking anyone, call us and tell us what's happening. We'll give you a straight steer on urgency and cost over the phone, not a script designed to get you to say yes. Call us on <a href={siteConfig.phoneHref}>{siteConfig.phoneDisplay}</a> or WhatsApp <a href={`https://wa.me/${siteConfig.whatsappNumberIntl}`}>{siteConfig.whatsappDisplay}</a> and we'll take it from there.</p>
